    pa:layer "manufacturer" ;
    pa:locator "p. 37" ;
    pa:quote "Flat-rate supplement for lack of ground clearance BF Ground clearance SL Protective field length without a supplement for lack of ground clearance ZF Supplement for lack of ground clearance The lump supplement for ground clearance under 120 mm is 150 mm." ;
    pa:relation pa:minimumDistanceParameter ;
    pa:sourceDocument "nanoscan3-manual" ;
    pa:value pa:Quantity_150_mm .

pa:manufacturer-st-0527 a pa:Statement ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo "strategy_b:manufacturer" ;
    pa:about pa:ProtectiveDevice_nanoScan3 ;
    pa:layer "manufacturer" ;
    pa:locator "p. 38" ;
    pa:quote "Minimum supplement for lack of ground clearance BF Ground clearance in mm ZF Supplement for lack of ground clearance in mm 5.3.10.3 Stopping distance SA The stopping distance is the sum of the following distances: O Braking distance of the vehicle O Distance covered during the response time of the safety laser scanner O Distance covered during the response time of the vehicle control (incl. signal propagation time) A vehicle’s braking distance does not increase linearly with increasing speed, but rather in a squared relationship." ;
    pa:relation pa:minimumDistanceRule ;
    pa:sourceDocument "nanoscan3-manual" ;
    pa:value "The stopping distance is the sum of the following distances" .

pa:manufacturer-st-0529 a pa:Statement ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo "strategy_b:manufacturer" ;
    pa:about pa:ProtectiveDevice_protective_field_length_of_the_nanoScan3 ;
    pa:layer "manufacturer" ;
    pa:locator "p. 39" ;
    pa:quote "PROJECT PLANNING 5 v Speed SA Stopping distance Z Supplements SL Protective field length for the relevant range of speeds SA = SBr + SAnF + SAnS where:" ;
    pa:relation pa:minimumDistanceRule ;
    pa:sourceDocument "nanoscan3-manual" ;
    pa:value "SA = SBr + SAnF + SAnS" .

pa:manufacturer-st-0530 a pa:Statement ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo "strategy_b:manufacturer" ;
    pa:about pa:ProtectiveDevice_protective_field_length_of_the_nanoScan3 ;
    pa:layer "manufacturer" ;
    pa:locator "p. 39" ;
    pa:quote "Vmax = maximum speed of the vehicle in the current monitoring case) Further topics O \"Response times\", page 133 5.3.10.4 Calculation example for the protective field length Calculation example for the protective field length SL SL = SA + TZ + ZR + ZF + ZB where:" ;
    pa:relation pa:minimumDistanceRule ;
    pa:sourceDocument "nanoscan3-manual" ;
    pa:value "SL = SA + TZ + ZR + ZF + ZB" .

pa:manufacturer-st-0531 a pa:Statement ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo "strategy_b:manufacturer" ;
    pa:about pa:ProtectiveDevice_nanoScan3_response_distance_SAnS ;
    pa:condition "If you define a number of monitoring cases with different protective fields" ;
    pa:layer "manufacturer" ;
    pa:locator "p. 39" ;
    pa:quote "SAnS = tR × Vmax where: o tR = response time of the safety laser scanner in seconds (s) o Vmax = maximum speed of the vehicle, from the vehicle documentation, in millimeters per second (mm/s) (If you define a number of monitoring cases with different protective fields: Vmax = maximum speed of the vehicle in the current monitoring case) Further topics O \"Response times\", page 133 5.3.10.4 Calculation example for the protective field length Calculation example for the protective field length SL SL = SA + TZ + ZR + ZF + ZB where:" ;
    pa:relation pa:minimumDistanceRule ;
    pa:sourceDocument "nanoscan3-manual" ;
    pa:value "SAnS = tR × Vmax" .

